<Project>
  <!--
    Central Package Management. Versions marked [checked 2026-08-22] were verified on NuGet
    when this suite was written. Everything else: verify at kickoff, then let Dependabot keep
    them current. Every pin here was re-verified against nuget.org on 2026-08-23 (kickoff);
    `Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.BannedApiAnalyzers 3.11.0` did not exist and was corrected - docs/24_ADR.md.
    WPF-UI stays pinned at exactly 4.3.0 (4.0.0-4.0.3, 4.1.0, 4.2.0 are deprecated
    on NuGet for critical bugs - see docs/22_WPFUI_SYNTAX.md).

    Swept against nuget.org on 2026-10-30. Three pins were left behind deliberately, and each one is a
    decision rather than an oversight:

      TraceEvent 3.2.4 (4.0.0 exists). This is the ETW heart, and the payload field names it exposes are
      absent from the package XML docs - they had to be found by reflecting over the assembly, and two of
      them are already known to read wrong (UpdIpV6TraceData, lower-case TcpIp* fields; docs/24_ADR.md).
      A major bump can rename a field and produce silently wrong byte attribution rather than a build
      error, and only the elevated Category=Admin round trip can prove otherwise. It gets its own PR.

      Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk 17.14.1 (18.11.0 exists). VSTest 18 changes how `dotnet test` runs, and the
      coverage format feeding SonarCloud changed in the same window. Bumping both at once makes a red run
      unattributable. Its own PR too.

      MaxMind.Db 4.2.0 (5.2.0 exists). Referenced by AppLedger.Infrastructure but called from no source
      file yet - GeoIP is a v0.5 item. Bumping a package nothing consumes buys nothing and risks something.

      CsWin32 0.3.298 (0.3.367 exists). Tried, and it is source-breaking in generated interop:
      SHGetKnownFolderPath now yields a CoTaskMemFreePWSTRSafeHandle instead of a PWSTR, and
      GetTokenInformation lost the four-argument overload - three call sites across KnownFolders and
      ProcessEnricher, which are the two files where a wrong P/Invoke produces a plausible number rather
      than an error. The KnownFolders change is an improvement worth taking (the SafeHandle removes a
      manual Marshal.FreeCoTaskMem and the unsafe block around it), and the token reads can only be proven
      by the elevated Category=Admin round trip. That makes it a migration, not a version sweep.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>true</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>
    <CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>true</CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- UI -->
    <PackageVersion Include="WPF-UI" Version="[4.3.0]" />                                  <!-- [checked 2026-08-22] pinned -->
    <PackageVersion Include="WPF-UI.DependencyInjection" Version="[4.3.0]" />
    <PackageVersion Include="ScottPlot.WPF" Version="5.1.59" />                             <!-- [checked 2026-08-22] -->
    <PackageVersion Include="CommunityToolkit.Mvvm" Version="8.4.2" />
    <PackageVersion Include="H.NotifyIcon.Wpf" Version="2.4.1" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Toolkit.Uwp.Notifications" Version="7.1.3" />
    <!-- Hosting / logging -->
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting" Version="10.0.14" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="10.0.14" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.Abstractions" Version="10.0.14" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Serilog" Version="4.4.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Serilog.Extensions.Hosting" Version="10.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Serilog.Sinks.File" Version="7.0.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Serilog.Settings.Configuration" Version="10.0.1" />
    <!-- Data -->
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Data.Sqlite" Version="10.0.14" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Dapper" Version="2.1.89" />
    <!-- The four SQLitePCLRaw transitive pins that lived here are gone as of 10.0.14, on the condition
         this comment itself set: Microsoft.Data.Sqlite 10.0.9 resolved SQLitePCLRaw 2.1.11 and so carried
         GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q (high), which was lifted by pinning 2.1.13 through
         CentralPackageTransitivePinningEnabled; 10.0.14 depends on bundle_e_sqlite3 and core 2.1.13
         directly, so the pins had become no-ops. Verified rather than assumed: with them removed, restore
         still resolves all four at 2.1.13 and the docs/18 vulnerability gate reports nothing
         (docs/24_ADR.md). Note for whoever edits this comment next: XML forbids a doubled hyphen inside a
         comment, so the switch names that gate passes cannot be written here. That is a finding of its own.

         They were also a hazard worth being rid of. A pin on a package nothing here references has to be
         kept in lockstep with whatever Microsoft.Data.Sqlite expects by hand - the 3.x line exists, and a
         bump to it on its own would have broken the provider rather than updated it. Transitive
         resolution now says what the version is, and the docs/18 vulnerability gate is what watches it. -->
    <!-- Windows / collection -->
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Diagnostics.Tracing.TraceEvent" Version="3.2.4" />  <!-- [checked 2026-08-22] -->
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.Windows.CsWin32" Version="0.3.298" />                      <!-- [checked 2026-08-22] -->
    <PackageVersion Include="MaxMind.Db" Version="4.2.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="NSec.Cryptography" Version="26.4.0" />                           <!-- minisign verification (docs/13) -->
    <!-- Packaging -->
    <PackageVersion Include="Velopack" Version="1.2.161" />                                   <!-- [checked 2026-08-22] -->
    <!-- Analyzers -->
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.BannedApiAnalyzers" Version="5.6.0" />  <!-- [checked 2026-08-23] the 3.11.0 this file first named has no stable release -->
    <!-- Tests -->
    <PackageVersion Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.14.1" />
    <PackageVersion Include="xunit" Version="2.9.3" />
    <PackageVersion Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="4.0.1" />
    <PackageVersion Include="NSubstitute" Version="6.2.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Shouldly" Version="4.3.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="coverlet.collector" Version="10.1.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
